### 4. RentalAmenityService
Imports needed: `java.time.LocalDateTime`, plus your existing `TimezoneConverter` and `BadRequestException`.
```java
@Override
@Transactional
public void upsertRentalBooking(TicketRequest req) {
    log.info("Upserting Rental Booking: bookingId: {}, inquiryId: {}, amenityId: {}, timezone: {}",
            req.getRentalBookingId(), req.getRentalInquiryId(), req.getAmenityId(), req.getTimezone());

    // Throws ValidationException for a null/blank/invalid IANA timezone
    TimezoneConverter.validateTimezone(req.getTimezone());

    LocalDateTime start = req.getRentalStartAt();   // local wall-clock at the venue (Jackson drops a trailing Z)
    LocalDateTime end = req.getRentalEndAt();

    if (start == null || end == null) {
        throw new BadRequestException("rentalStartAt and rentalEndAt are required");
    }
    if (!end.isAfter(start)) {
        throw new BadRequestException("rentalEndAt must be after rentalStartAt");
    }
    rejectDstGap(start, "rentalStartAt", req.getTimezone());
    rejectDstGap(end, "rentalEndAt", req.getTimezone());

    // Convert in place: after this the request holds UTC, which is what the DAO stores
    req.setRentalStartAt(TimezoneConverter.toUtc(start, req.getTimezone()).toLocalDateTime());
    req.setRentalEndAt(TimezoneConverter.toUtc(end, req.getTimezone()).toLocalDateTime());

    rentalAmenityDao.upsertRentalBooking(req);
}

private void rejectDstGap(LocalDateTime dateTime, String field, String timezone) {
    if (TimezoneConverter.isInDstGap(dateTime, timezone)) {
        throw new BadRequestException(field + " " + dateTime + " does not exist in " + timezone
                + " because of daylight saving. Please choose a different time.");
    }
}
```

